.DS_Store

# runs/ and registry/ are evidence, not build output — they are committed on purpose.

# Claude Code local state (agent worktrees, etc.) — not part of the repo.
.claude/

# --- what stays out of this repository, and on WHOSE say-so ---------------------------
#
# gnostrich/common-ground is PUBLIC (checked 2026-08-05, GitHub API: "private": false).
# Anything committed here is published.
#
# ROHAN'S INSTRUCTION, in his words:
#   "NEVER commit them or the corpus" (the Aristotle API keys and the Lean corpus)
#   "Do NOT commit the user's proprietary Lean corpus into the repo without first
#    confirming repo visibility with Rohan"
# Visibility is now confirmed: the repo is public, so the corpus stays out. That much is
# his rule and it is quoted rather than paraphrased.
#
# CLAUDE'S ENGINEERING JUDGEMENT, which is NOT his rule and is labelled as mine:
#   pool.jsonl and corpus.snapshot are derived from that corpus and carry its nu-strings
#   verbatim, so publishing them publishes the corpus by another route. They are also pure
#   functions of (corpus, seed, code), so keeping them out costs rebuild time and no
#   information. If Rohan wants them committed, that is his call to make and it overrides
#   this line.
#
# An earlier version of this file stated the above as a numbered "hard constraint" and a
# keepalive prompt I had written myself repeated it back as though it came from Rohan. It
# did not. Treating my own inference as his instruction is how a project acquires rules
# nobody agreed to, and it blocked the journal-durability fix for hours.
#
# corpus.local.json is the ONE file that names where a corpus lives — repo roots, export
# paths, excluded conversation ids. It is what makes this mechanism forkable: the template
# `seed/CORPUS.example.json` is committed, the real pointer is not, so anyone can take the
# engine without taking the shape of somebody's disk. tests/test_corpus_sources.py asserts
# this line still holds, because the seam is only real while the pointer stays out.
corpus.local.json
runs/pool.jsonl
runs/corpus.snapshot
runs/proposer.journal.jsonl
runs/proposer.control.json
runs/proposer.status.json
